WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.858
Daniel was eating lunch with his grandmother and her friends at the retirement community.

2
00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:16.554
"Daniel does wonderful magic tricks," Grandma said proudly to Mr. Hudson and Mrs. Ross.

3
00:00:16.555 --> 00:00:24.346
"Would you like to see one?" Daniel picked up his spoon and wiped it off.

4
00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:33.282
"I will now use my magic powers to bend this spoon."

5
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:42.767
Daniel focused on the spoon, which slowly bent in his hands.

6
00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:47.582
"Such a clever boy!" Grandma said.

7
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:51.344
But Mr. Hudson wasn't impressed.

8
00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:59.642
"You need to work on concealing the spoon's handle.

9
00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:05.563
A magician must be aware of how his tricks look from every angle.

10
00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:09.371
I could see what you were doing over here."

11
00:01:09.372 --> 00:01:14.773
Daniel sighed. "Are you a magician?"

12
00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:20.472
Mr. Hudson nodded. "What's your favorite trick?"

13
00:01:20.473 --> 00:01:23.534
Daniel's face lit up.

14
00:01:23.535 --> 00:01:28.716
"I love all kinds of magic, especially big illusions!

15
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:34.613
It would be fun to make someone float above a table."

16
00:01:34.614 --> 00:01:43.505
"Levitation tricks require special equipment that amateur magicians don't have," Mr. Hudson said.

17
00:01:43.506 --> 00:01:48.993
"Things like platforms that rise in the air.

18
00:01:48.994 --> 00:01:55.060
But I think card tricks and other close-up magic require more skill."

19
00:01:55.061 --> 00:01:57.868
He took out a coin.

20
00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:04.279
"My favorite tricks involve teleportation—like moving coins from place to place."

21
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.525
Mr. Hudson made the coin vanish from one hand.

22
00:02:08.526 --> 00:02:14.781
He pulled it out from behind Daniel's ear with his other hand.

23
00:02:14.782 --> 00:02:19.779
Daniel shook his head. "How did you do that?"

24
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.568
"Practice!" Mr. Hudson winked.

25
00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:32.572
"I've always admired escape artists, though their routines make me so nervous," Mrs. Ross said.

26
00:02:32.573 --> 00:02:37.975
"Especially when someone is handcuffed or tied inside a tank of water."

27
00:02:37.976 --> 00:02:42.361
"Don't worry," Mr. Hudson said.

28
00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:50.961
"An assistant slips the magician the keys to the handcuffs or uses knots that are easy to untie.

29
00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:57.775
The magician escapes quickly but stays underwater for suspense."

30
00:02:57.776 --> 00:03:03.098
"I still wouldn't want Daniel trying that!" Grandma said.

31
00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:09.204
"I prefer classic tricks like pulling a rabbit out of a hat."

32
00:03:09.205 --> 00:03:13.684
"Nobody does that anymore, Grandma.

33
00:03:13.685 --> 00:03:18.323
Using animals in magic acts is considered cruel.

34
00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:23.796
Magicians pull other things out of hats today—like bowling balls!"

35
00:03:23.797 --> 00:03:30.390
"The item is often hidden in a secret compartment," Mr. Hudson explained.

36
00:03:30.391 --> 00:03:37.847
"The magician sets his hat over the compartment and pulls the object through an opening in the hat."

37
00:03:37.848 --> 00:03:41.818
"I'm just a beginner," Daniel said.

38
00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:45.648
"All those tricks take lots of practice!"

39
00:03:45.649 --> 00:03:50.943
Daniel was determined to outwit Mr. Hudson.

40
00:03:50.944 --> 00:03:57.555
So the next time he visited Grandma, he brought an assistant, his friend Joaquin.

41
00:03:57.556 --> 00:04:04.899
"There's another kind of magic we didn't discuss," Daniel said as Joaquin blindfolded him.

42
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.932
"Mind reading."

43
00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:14.701
Joaquin invited Mrs. Ross to hand him any item from her purse.

44
00:04:14.702 --> 00:04:21.173
"I'm thinking about this object." Joaquin paused.

45
00:04:21.174 --> 00:04:24.119
"Read my mind."

46
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.599
"Wallet," Daniel said.

47
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:34.241
"You're right!" Mrs. Ross handed Joaquin something else.

48
00:04:34.242 --> 00:04:42.700
"I'm thinking about this object." Joaquin paused for a few seconds.

49
00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:46.689
"Read my mind."

50
00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:52.818
"Comb," Daniel replied.

51
00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:58.278
"Wonderful!" Mr. Hudson applauded.

52
00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:05.347
"Magicians and their assistants usually have code words for different items, but I'm puzzled.

53
00:05:05.348 --> 00:05:09.159
Joaquin said the same thing both times.

54
00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:14.052
If you did the trick again, I could probably figure it out."

55
00:05:14.053 --> 00:05:19.075
Daniel removed his blindfold.

56
00:05:19.076 --> 00:05:24.212
"That's why we're not repeating it!" he said.

57
00:05:24.213 --> 00:05:30.247
"Won't you read my mind just once?" Grandma pleaded.

58
00:05:30.248 --> 00:05:34.932
"Sure, that's easy." Daniel grinned.

59
00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:40.913
"You're thinking, 'Such a clever boy!'"

